# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and machine-local configuration
#
# Nothing in here is checked in even if it looks harmless today, because the
# cost of noticing a leak after the fact is much higher than the cost of a
# second copy of a config file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MCP server configuration. Holds absolute paths to this machine's tools, and is
# the usual place an API key or token ends up.
.mcp.json
.mcp.*.json
mcp.json

# Per-machine agent and editor settings. The shared half of a .claude folder can
# be force-added later if it is ever worth sharing.
.claude/
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Credentials of every shape.
#
# These are deliberately NOT bare substring globs. On Windows git matches
# gitignore case-insensitively, so a pattern like *token* would silently refuse
# to track a future Token.h or Tokenizer.cpp, and this project is reverse
# engineering a script VM where those are likely file names. A silently
# untracked source file is a worse failure than a slightly narrower net, so
# every pattern here is anchored to a whole name or a real extension.
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.txt
secrets.ini
*.secret
*.secrets
credentials.json
credentials.txt
credentials.ini
.credentials
*.token
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.npmrc
*.pwd
auth.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# loader/build is created and wiped wholesale by the build scripts, so there is
# never a reason to track any of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
loader/build/
build/
out/
bin/
obj/

# MSVC and linker leftovers, in case a build is ever run somewhere else.
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlog
*.res
*.sbr
*.bsc

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CMakeScripts/
Makefile
*.cmake.in

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reverse engineering working files
#
# The IDA database lives next to FFX.exe in the Steam folder, not here, but a
# stray copy must not be committed. It is large and it contains the game's own
# code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.i64
*.idb
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.nam
*.til
*.asm.txt

# Extracted game assets. Everything the tools unpack out of the shipped VBF
# archives is the publisher's content and does not belong in this repo. Only the
# scripts that read the formats, and the notes about them, are ours.
extracted/
assets/
dump/
dumps/
*.vbf
*.ebp
*.mgrp
*.bin.dec

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.vcxproj.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*~
scratch/
tmp/
